# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the NashDom project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency to package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency and its transitive dependencies
- Used npm (the project's package manager) to ensure consistent dependency resolution

### 2. Modified Root Layout Component
**File:** `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`

Added the Analytics component following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Imported the Analytics component: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, after the existing Providers and Toaster components

The Analytics component was placed after all other body content to ensure it doesn't interfere with the existing application structure and follows best practices for third-party scripts.

## Implementation Details

This implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide for Next.js App Router (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart on 2026-06-12).

The Analytics component will:
- Automatically track page views and user interactions
- Send analytics data to Vercel when the app is deployed
- Work in both development and production environments
- Have no visible UI impact on the application

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ **Build Verification**: Successfully built the project with `npm run build --turbopack`
   - Build completed without errors
   - All 15 static and dynamic routes generated successfully
   - TypeScript compilation passed

2. ✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint`
   - No new linting errors introduced by the Analytics integration
   - The layout.tsx file passed all linting checks
   - Existing linting issues in other files are unrelated to this change

3. ✅ **Dependency Installation**: Lock file updated correctly
   - package-lock.json properly updated with new dependencies
   - Ensures consistent installations across environments

## Next Steps for Deployment

To activate analytics tracking on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Navigate to the Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Select the project and click "Enable" to activate analytics
4. After deployment, verify tracking by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Notes

- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't affect application performance
- Analytics data will only be collected when the app is deployed on Vercel
- The implementation preserves all existing functionality and code structure
- No breaking changes were introduced
